&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;...&amp;quot;:&lt;/code&gt; key in the second line only abbreviates this page. Real lines repeat all fields.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>How it works</title><link>https://circleci-labs.github.io/runner-job-wrapper/docs/reference/how-it-works/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://circleci-labs.github.io/runner-job-wrapper/docs/reference/how-it-works/</guid><description>
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="how-command_prefix-invokes-the-wrapper"&gt;How command_prefix invokes the wrapper&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="how-command_prefix-invokes-the-wrapper"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#how-command_prefix-invokes-the-wrapper" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;With this runner config:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;runner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;command_prefix&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;/usr/local/bin/circleci-job-wrapper&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the runner executes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;/usr/local/bin/circleci-job-wrapper &amp;lt;task-agent-path&amp;gt; &amp;lt;agent args...&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;with the job&amp;rsquo;s built-in environment (&lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_*&lt;/code&gt;) added and the task token on stdin. The wrapper:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starts the task agent as a child with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;amp;0&lt;/code&gt;, so stdin is the very same pipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;While the job already runs, resolves the host identity and writes &lt;code&gt;job_start&lt;/code&gt; and the state file. The cost to job start-up is one &lt;code&gt;fork&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Waits for the child. If the wrapper itself gets &lt;code&gt;SIGTERM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SIGINT&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;SIGHUP&lt;/code&gt;, it forwards the signal to the child.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writes &lt;code&gt;job_end&lt;/code&gt;, removes the state file, and exits with the child&amp;rsquo;s exit code (&lt;code&gt;128+n&lt;/code&gt; for a signalled child).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every helper command the wrapper runs has &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;/dev/null&lt;/code&gt;, so it can never take the task token from the agent&amp;rsquo;s stdin. The wrapper never changes the job&amp;rsquo;s environment, umask or process group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="overhead"&gt;Overhead&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="overhead"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#overhead" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;About 6 ms per job. The agent is spawned before any telemetry runs. Logging is best effort: every logging failure is swallowed, and the wrapper is silent unless &lt;code&gt;CCI_JOBLOG_DEBUG&lt;/code&gt; is set. It needs bash 4 or later and POSIX utilities, with no &lt;code&gt;jq&lt;/code&gt;, no daemon and no Python.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="agent_status-is-not-the-job-result"&gt;agent_status is not the job result&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="agent_status-is-not-the-job-result"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#agent_status-is-not-the-job-result" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The task agent exits 0 even when the job fails or is cancelled from the UI. So &lt;code&gt;completed&lt;/code&gt; only means the agent process exited 0. Take the job result from the CircleCI span (&lt;code&gt;com.circleci.job.status&lt;/code&gt;) or, on the host, from the task agent&amp;rsquo;s own &amp;ldquo;Reporting task end.&amp;rdquo; log line (see &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/runner-job-wrapper/docs/send-the-data/ship-with-alloy/"&gt;Ship with Grafana Alloy&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;cancelled&lt;/code&gt; only means the wrapper received &lt;code&gt;TERM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;INT&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;HUP&lt;/code&gt;, for example because the runner is stopping a task.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="signals"&gt;Signals&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="signals"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#signals" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When the runner stops a task, it sends &lt;code&gt;SIGTERM&lt;/code&gt; to the &lt;code&gt;command_prefix&lt;/code&gt; process only, not the process group. It sends &lt;code&gt;SIGKILL&lt;/code&gt; to the whole process group after 10 s, or immediately with &lt;code&gt;enable_unsafe_retries&lt;/code&gt;. So:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Signal forwarding (on by default) is required. Otherwise the agent never sees the &lt;code&gt;SIGTERM&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the agent has not exited within 10 s, the wrapper is killed too and &lt;code&gt;job_end&lt;/code&gt; is lost. Consumers must tolerate a &lt;code&gt;job_start&lt;/code&gt; without a &lt;code&gt;job_end&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A cancel from the CircleCI UI is handled by the agent itself (exit 0, no signal), so it shows as &lt;code&gt;completed&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="stdin"&gt;stdin&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="stdin"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#stdin" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The task token stays on the agent&amp;rsquo;s stdin. The wrapper never reads or redirects it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="environment-the-runner-provides"&gt;Environment the runner provides&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="environment-the-runner-provides"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#environment-the-runner-provides" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Verified on machine runner 3.1.14, these built-in variables reach the &lt;code&gt;command_prefix&lt;/code&gt; process (names only):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_BRANCH&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_BUILD_NUM&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_BUILD_URL&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_JOB&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_NODE_INDEX&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_NODE_TOTAL&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_ORGANIZATION_ID&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_PIPELINE_ID&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_PROJECT_ID&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_PROJECT_REPONAME&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_PROJECT_USERNAME&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_REPOSITORY_URL&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_SHA1&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_USERNAME&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_WORKFLOW_ID&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_WORKFLOW_JOB_ID&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;CIRCLE_WORKFLOW_WORKSPACE_ID&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no resource class, pipeline number or PR number, so those event fields stay empty unless you supply them. For the resource class, see &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/runner-job-wrapper/docs/configure/configuration/#resource-class"&gt;Configuration&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="multiple-runners-on-one-host"&gt;Multiple runners on one host&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="multiple-runners-on-one-host"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#multiple-runners-on-one-host" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Several runner agents share one wrapper, one log file and one cache. Each event carries its &lt;code&gt;runner_name&lt;/code&gt;, and each runner has its own state file. See &lt;a href="https://circleci-labs.github.io/runner-job-wrapper/docs/get-started/install/#several-runner-agents-on-one-host"&gt;Install&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>